<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wittenberg</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Lutherstadt Wittenberg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wittenberg, officially Lutherstadt Wittenberg, is a town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbe">Elbe</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony-anhalt">Saxony-Anhalt</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. It was the seat of the Ascanian dukes of Saxe-Wittenberg and then of the Wettin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-elector">electors</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a>, whose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/university-of-wittenberg">University of Wittenberg</a> was founded in 1502. There <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther">Martin Luther</a> published his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ninety-five-theses">Ninety-five Theses</a> in 1517, beginning the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a>. Its Luther memorials are a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wittenberg.jpg" alt="Wittenberg" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Toniklemm · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stadtkirche_Marktplatz_Schlosskirche_Wittenberg_Luftbild_2024_Toni_Klemm.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
